esc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":0,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 177.2%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 1.07"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":112.81,"default_fair_val":112.81,"premium_pct":-69.3,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":17.3,"pe_forward":15.2,"pb_trailing":-3.4,"pb_forward":-3.1,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":2.1,"fcf_to_ev":8.84,"fcf_to_mcap":12.14,"liab_to_assets":177.2,"cash_to_assets":40.3,"current_ratio":1.07,"roe":-19.9,"roa":15.4,"moat":{"ticker":"DBX","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 的品牌在雲端儲存領域具有相當的辨識度，尤其在個人用戶和小型企業中，其易用性和可靠性建立了良好的聲譽。然而，面對 Google Drive、Microsoft OneDrive 等科技巨頭的激烈競爭，以及蘋果 iCloud 的生態整合優勢，Dropbox 的品牌定價權受到一定限制。雖然其品牌價值能支撐一定的溢價，但難以形成絕對的價格主導地位。其核心競爭力在於簡潔的用戶體驗和跨平台同步能力，這使其在特定用戶群體中保持了較強的黏性，但與頂級科技品牌的品牌護城河相比，仍有差距。","comment_en":"Dropbox's brand has considerable recognition in the cloud storage sector, particularly among individual users and small businesses, where its ease of use and reliability have built a strong reputation. However, facing intense competition from tech giants like Google Drive and Microsoft OneDrive, as well as the ecosystem integration advantages of Apple's iCloud, Dropbox's brand pricing power is somewhat constrained. While its brand equity can support a certain premium, it's difficult to establish an absolute price leadership. Its core competitiveness lies in its simple user experience and cross-platform synchronization capabilities, which maintain strong stickiness within specific user groups. Nevertheless, compared to the brand moats of top-tier tech companies, there is still a gap."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 作為一家軟體公司，其核心技術主要依賴於演算法和軟體架構，而非具有高度專利壁壘的硬體或製藥。雖然公司可能擁有與檔案同步、儲存優化等相關的專利，但這些專利在面對大型科技公司的廣泛技術儲備和快速迭代能力時，其獨特性和持久性相對較弱。軟體行業的技術更新換代迅速，專利保護的有效性往往受到挑戰。此外，該行業的監管環境相對寬鬆，較少依賴特許經營權或嚴格的監管批准來建立壁壘。","comment_en":"As a software company, Dropbox's core technology relies primarily on algorithms and software architecture, rather than highly patented hardware or pharmaceuticals. While the company may hold patents related to file synchronization, storage optimization, etc., their uniqueness and longevity are relatively weak when faced with the extensive technological reserves and rapid iteration capabilities of large tech corporations. The software industry experiences rapid technological evolution, and the effectiveness of patent protection is often challenged. Furthermore, the regulatory environment in this sector is relatively lenient, relying less on exclusive licenses or strict regulatory approvals to establish barriers."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於個人用戶而言，從 Dropbox 遷移到其他雲端儲存服務的轉換成本相對較低，主要涉及重新上傳和下載檔案。然而，對於深度整合 Dropbox 的企業用戶，特別是那些依賴其 API 進行工作流程自動化或與其他應用程式整合的用戶，轉換成本會顯著提高。這些用戶不僅需要遷移大量的歷史數據，還可能需要重新配置或尋找替代的整合方案，這會耗費時間和資源。因此，在企業級市場，Dropbox 具備一定的客戶黏性，形成了一定的轉換壁壘。","comment_en":"For individual users, the switching costs from Dropbox to other cloud storage services are relatively low, mainly involving re-uploading and downloading files. However, for enterprise users who have deeply integrated Dropbox, especially those relying on its API for workflow automation or integration with other applications, the switching costs increase significantly. These users not only need to migrate substantial historical data but may also need to reconfigure or find alternative integration solutions, consuming time and resources. Therefore, in the enterprise market, Dropbox possesses a certain degree of customer stickiness, forming a moderate switching barrier."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 的網絡效應主要體現在其協作功能上。當越來越多的用戶和團隊使用 Dropbox 進行檔案共享和協作時，其價值會隨之增加，因為這使得團隊成員之間更容易溝通和共享資訊。例如，在一個項目團隊中，如果大多數成員都在使用 Dropbox，那麼新加入的成員也更有可能選擇 Dropbox 以便無縫接入。然而，與社交網絡或市場平台類型的網絡效應相比，Dropbox 的網絡效應相對較弱，其核心價值更多地建立在單一用戶的檔案儲存和同步需求上，而非由用戶間互動產生的強烈正反饋循環。","comment_en":"Dropbox's network effects are primarily evident in its collaboration features. As more users and teams use Dropbox for file sharing and collaboration, its value increases, making it easier for team members to communicate and share information. For instance, within a project team, if most members are using Dropbox, new joiners are more likely to choose Dropbox for seamless integration. However, compared to network effects in social networks or marketplace platforms, Dropbox's network effects are relatively weaker. Its core value is more rooted in individual users' file storage and synchronization needs, rather than a strong positive feedback loop generated by user interactions."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"作為一家領先的雲端儲存服務提供商，Dropbox 受益於規模經濟效應。其龐大的用戶基礎和數據中心規模，使其在採購硬體、電力、頻寬等方面具有較強的議價能力，從而降低了單位儲存成本。這種規模優勢有助於其在價格上與競爭對手抗衡，並為進一步的服務擴張提供支持。然而，與亞馬遜 AWS、微軟 Azure 等基礎設施級別的雲端服務巨頭相比，Dropbox 的規模優勢主要集中在應用層的儲存服務，而非底層基礎設施的成本控制，因此其成本優勢的範圍相對有限。","comment_en":"As a leading cloud storage service provider, Dropbox benefits from economies of scale. Its vast user base and data center scale give it strong bargaining power in procuring hardware, electricity, and bandwidth, thereby reducing unit storage costs. This scale advantage helps it compete on price with rivals and supports further service expansion. However, compared to infrastructure-level cloud service giants like Amazon AWS and Microsoft Azure, Dropbox's scale advantage is mainly concentrated in application-layer storage services, rather than cost control at the underlying infrastructure level, thus its cost advantage is relatively limited in scope."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 的業務模式是全球性的數位服務，其核心資產是軟體平台和數據中心基礎設施，這些資產的地理位置並非其主要的競爭壁壘。公司在全球範圍內運營，以服務全球用戶，但並不存在依賴特定地理位置的獨特資源或市場。其競爭優勢更多地來自於技術、品牌和用戶網絡，而非地理位置的稀缺性或特殊性。因此，在這一維度上，Dropbox 的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"Dropbox's business model is a global digital service. Its core assets are its software platform and data center infrastructure, and the geographical location of these assets is not its primary competitive barrier. The company operates globally to serve users worldwide, but there are no unique resources or markets dependent on specific geographical locations. Its competitive advantages stem more from technology, brand, and user networks, rather than the scarcity or uniqueness of its geographical locations. Therefore, on this dimension, Dropbox's moat is very weak."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 在提升運營效率方面取得了顯著進展，尤其是在將免費用戶轉化為付費用戶以及優化基礎設施成本方面。公司近年來專注於提高盈利能力，通過精簡產品線和聚焦核心業務，有效控制了營運費用。其持續的自由現金流（FCF TTM: $915.2M）證明了其業務模式的健康和運營的有效性。儘管面臨激烈的市場競爭，Dropbox 仍能維持較高的利潤率和現金流生成能力，這體現了其在軟體服務領域的運營效率。","comment_en":"Dropbox has made significant progress in improving operational efficiency, particularly in converting free users to paid subscribers and optimizing infrastructure costs. The company has focused on enhancing profitability in recent years, effectively controlling operating expenses by streamlining its product lines and focusing on core businesses. Its consistent free cash flow (FCF TTM: $915.2M) demonstrates the health of its business model and the effectiveness of its operations. Despite facing intense market competition, Dropbox continues to maintain healthy profit margins and cash flow generation capabilities, reflecting its operational efficiency in the software services sector."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 的資本配置策略近年來趨於保守和務實，重點在於回購股票和償還債務，以提升股東價值和降低財務風險。公司現金儲備相對充足（現金 $1,142.2M），但負債水平也較高（負債 $3,955.8M），這限制了其進行大規模激進投資的能力。雖然回購股票和減少債務是穩健的資本配置方式，但相較於那些能夠持續進行高回報率的研發投入或戰略併購的公司，其增長潛力可能受到一定影響。管理層在維持財務穩健與尋求增長之間尋求平衡。","comment_en":"Dropbox's capital allocation strategy has become more conservative and pragmatic in recent years, focusing on share buybacks and debt repayment to enhance shareholder value and reduce financial risk. The company has a relatively ample cash reserve ($1,142.2M cash), but also a significant debt level ($3,955.8M liabilities), which limits its capacity for large-scale aggressive investments. While share buybacks and debt reduction are prudent capital allocation methods, its growth potential might be somewhat affected compared to companies that can consistently invest in R&D or strategic acquisitions with high rates of return. Management seeks a balance between maintaining financial stability and pursuing growth."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 在客戶留存方面表現穩健，尤其是在其付費客戶群體中。一旦用戶習慣了 Dropbox 的工作流程和跨設備同步體驗，且其數據儲存在平台上，遷移的意願就會降低。公司通過不斷優化產品功能、提升用戶體驗以及提供差異化的企業級解決方案，來鞏固現有客戶關係。然而，免費用戶的流失率可能相對較高，因為他們更容易受到免費增值服務的吸引或尋找替代品。總體而言，其付費客戶的留存率是其業務穩定性的關鍵支撐。","comment_en":"Dropbox demonstrates solid customer retention, particularly within its paid customer base. Once users become accustomed to Dropbox's workflow and cross-device synchronization experience, and their data is stored on the platform, their willingness to switch decreases. The company solidifies existing customer relationships by continuously optimizing product features, enhancing user experience, and offering differentiated enterprise-level solutions. However, the churn rate among free users might be relatively high, as they are more susceptible to attractive freemium services or readily seek alternatives. Overall, the retention rate of its paying customers is a key support for its business stability."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Dropbox 的業務模式具有一定的持久性，雲端儲存和協作需求是數位時代的剛性需求。然而，其面臨的挑戰在於技術的快速變革和來自大型科技公司的激烈競爭。雖然其核心功能相對穩定，但持續的創新和適應市場變化是保持持久性的關鍵。與那些擁有獨特專利、強大品牌或網絡效應的企業相比，Dropbox 的護城河深度相對較淺，其持久性在很大程度上取決於其持續創新和維持用戶黏性的能力。其商業模式更接近於一種高效的服務提供商，而非擁有極強定價權的特許經營權。","comment_en":"Dropbox's business model possesses a degree of durability, as cloud storage and collaboration needs are essential demands in the digital age. However, the challenges it faces lie in rapid technological change and intense competition from large technology companies. While its core functionalities are relatively stable, continuous innovation and adaptation to market changes are crucial for maintaining durability. Compared to companies with unique patents, strong brands, or network effects, Dropbox's moat depth is relatively shallow. Its durability largely depends on its ability to continuously innovate and maintain user stickiness. Its business model is more akin to an efficient service provider rather than a franchise with exceptionally strong pricing power."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Dropbox 的經濟護城河呈現出混合的特徵。其品牌知名度和在特定用戶群體中的黏性（M1, M9）構成了一定的壁壘，尤其是在企業級市場，轉換成本（M3）也提供了一定的保護。規模經濟（M5）和運營效率（M7）使其能夠在成本上保持競爭力。然而，其專利和監管壁壘（M2）非常薄弱，網絡效應（M4）也相對有限。資本配置（M8）相對穩健但缺乏進取性，地理資產（M6）幾乎不存在護城河。整體而言，Dropbox 處於一個競爭激烈的市場，其護城河深度尚可，但距離巴菲特所青睞的、具有強大特許經營權或收費橋性質的企業尚有距離，更像是一個高效的服務提供商。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Dropbox's economic moat exhibits mixed characteristics. Its brand recognition and stickiness within specific user segments (M1, M9) form a certain barrier, especially in the enterprise market where switching costs (M3) also provide some protection. Economies of scale (M5) and operational efficiency (M7) enable it to remain competitive on cost. However, its patent and regulatory barriers (M2) are very weak, and network effects (M4) are relatively limited. Capital allocation (M8) is prudent but lacks aggressiveness, and geographical assets (M6) offer virtually no moat. Overall, Dropbox operates in a highly competitive market with a moderate moat depth. It falls short of being the type of business with strong franchise or toll-bridge characteristics that Warren Buffett favors, appearing more as an efficient service provider.","evidenceHash":"5e34113e2cac73a133696c06a6e04b1e93186f30a70c2443a6d7673ad283579d","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"5e34113e2cac73a133696c06a6e04b1e93186f30a70c2443a6d7673ad283579d","currentEvidenceHash":"5e34113e2cac73a133696c06a6e04b1e93186f30a70c2443a6d7673ad283579d"},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T14:18:43.603Z","evidenceHash":"9303448a360e2467e6f3676c7216a9ffb78195926011ce0f7350b3156919b449"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T14:18:43.603Z","evidenceHash":"9303448a360e2467e6f3676c7216a9ffb78195926011ce0f7350b3156919b449"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/DBX.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/DBX.png","website":"https://www.dropbox.com","ceo":"Andrew W. Houston","full_time_employees":"2113","description":"Dropbox, Inc. engages in providing file backup, sync, and sharing solutions. Its products include Dropbox, Dropbox Reply, Dropbox Sign, Dropbox Reclaim.ai, Dropbox Dash, Dropbox DocSend, Dropbox Fax, and Dropbox Early access. It operates through the United States and International geographical segments. The company was founded by Andrew W. Houston and Arash Ferdowsi in May 2007 and is headquartered in San Francisco, CA.","description_en":"Dropbox, Inc. engages in providing file backup, sync, and sharing solutions. Its products include Dropbox, Dropbox Reply, Dropbox Sign, Dropbox Reclaim.ai, Dropbox Dash, Dropbox DocSend, Dropbox Fax, and Dropbox Early access. It operates through the United States and International geographical segments. The company was founded by Andrew W. Houston and Arash Ferdowsi in May 2007